\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The decomposition, on frozen test splits. Repair (blue, above the axis) and breakage (orange, below) are of comparable size for a standard verify--refine workflow, so the net effect (black, 95\% CI) sits near zero or below it --- the quantity the literature reports is a difference of two large terms. Protecting the incumbent answer removes the lower term entirely (breakage $0.000$ in all cells) and the same machinery becomes a small, reliable gain. Both panels share an axis.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:decomposition}{{1}{4}{The decomposition, on frozen test splits. Repair (blue, above the axis) and breakage (orange, below) are of comparable size for a standard verify--refine workflow, so the net effect (black, 95\% CI) sits near zero or below it --- the quantity the literature reports is a difference of two large terms. Protecting the incumbent answer removes the lower term entirely (breakage $0.000$ in all cells) and the same machinery becomes a small, reliable gain. Both panels share an axis}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Frozen test splits, 150 tasks per family, 3 execution seeds. Baselines are the strongest single-call structure per family (\texttt  {direct} for code, \texttt  {cot} for math). Intervals are stratified paired bootstrap 95\% CIs. \emph  {vanilla} is generate$\to $verify$\to $refine with up to 3 iterations; \emph  {protected} is the same loop with a temperature-0 incumbent that is replaced only on verifier rejection.}}{4}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:parti}{{1}{4}{Frozen test splits, 150 tasks per family, 3 execution seeds. Baselines are the strongest single-call structure per family (\texttt {direct} for code, \texttt {cot} for math). Intervals are stratified paired bootstrap 95\% CIs. \emph {vanilla} is generate$\to $verify$\to $refine with up to 3 iterations; \emph {protected} is the same loop with a temperature-0 incumbent that is replaced only on verifier rejection}{table.1}{}}
